Chapter: DropdownOptions
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites UI chapter Dropdown
  cites UI chapter Widget
  cites UI chapter KeyInput

 Dropdown is reached by DiffusionApp through SettingsPanel, which calls
 dropdown-widget for every SfDropdown field, so the closed trigger is
 live. Opening, filtering, highlighting and confirming are reached by
 nothing, which is where the questions are: a control that cannot be
 opened from the keyboard is the same shape of defect TextField and
 TreeView both carried.

 Eleven options against a visible cap of eight, so the cap is exercised
 rather than assumed, and a filter that selects six of the eleven, so the
 highlight is asked in a space that is NOT the full option list. Those two
 are the cases where an index into the visible options and an index into
 all of them stop coinciding.

 We say:

Section: Reading

  at : WidgetNode, Integer -> WidgetNode
  at (w) (i) = list-at (w.wn-children) i

  payload : WidgetNode -> Text
  payload (w) = when w.wn-kind
    is WkLabel (t) -> "[" & t & "]"
    is WkButton (t) -> "<" & t & ">"
    is WkGauge (v) (m) -> "gauge"
    is WkInput (t) (c) -> "input(" & t & ")"
    is WkSeparator -> "sep"
    is WkPanel -> "panel"
    is WkCustom (tag) -> tag

  join : List Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  join (xs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else join xs (i + 1) n (acc & (if i > 0 then "," else "") & list-at xs i)

  show-opts : List Text -> Text
  show-opts (xs) = join xs 0 (list-length xs) ""

  yn : Boolean -> Text
  yn (b) = if b then "yes" else "no"

Section: The options under test

  opts : Integer -> List Text
  opts (x) = ["alpha", "bravo", "charlie", "delta", "echo", "foxtrot",
              "golf", "hotel", "india", "juliet", "kilo"]

  base : Integer -> DropdownState
  base (x) = dropdown-new "dd" (opts 0)

  opened : Integer -> DropdownState
  opened (x) = dropdown-toggle (base 0)

  navd : DropdownState, Integer -> DropdownState
  navd (dd) (n) = if n <= 0 then dd else navd (dropdown-nav-down dd) (n - 1)

Section: Selection text

 A dropdown with nothing chosen must say so rather than naming an option,
 and an index outside the option list must answer empty rather than
 reading past the end.

  line-selected : Text =
    "selected: none=[" & dropdown-selected-text (base 0)
    & "] index2=[" & dropdown-selected-text (dropdown-with-selected "dd" (opts 0) 2)
    & "] beyond=[" & dropdown-selected-text (dropdown-with-selected "dd" (opts 0) 99)
    & "] negative=[" & dropdown-selected-text (dropdown-with-selected "dd" (opts 0) (0 - 1)) & "]"

Section: What is visible

 Eleven options, a cap of eight. The filter takes every option containing
 the letter o, which is six of the eleven and not a prefix of them.

  line-cap : Text =
    "cap: options=" & show (list-length (opts 0))
    & " max-visible=" & show ((base 0).dd-max-visible)
    & " visible=" & show (list-length (dropdown-visible-options (base 0)))

  line-visible : Text =
    "visible: " & show-opts (dropdown-visible-options (base 0))

  line-filtered : Text =
    "filtered o: " & show-opts (dropdown-visible-options (dropdown-set-filter (base 0) "o"))

Section: Highlight and confirm

 The highlight indexes the VISIBLE options, so confirming has to map it
 back through the full list. Under a filter those two spaces differ, which
 is the case that tells a correct mapping from one that returns the
 highlight as an option index.

  line-nav-clamp : Text =
    "nav: down x3=" & show ((navd (opened 0) 3).dd-highlight)
    & " down x20=" & show ((navd (opened 0) 20).dd-highlight)
    & " of visible " & show (list-length (dropdown-visible-options (opened 0)))
    & " up-from-zero=" & show ((dropdown-nav-up (opened 0)).dd-highlight)

  line-confirm : Text =
    "confirm: unfiltered down x3=[" & dropdown-selected-text (dropdown-confirm (navd (opened 0) 3)) & "]"

 Filtered, the visible list is bravo echo foxtrot golf hotel kilo.
 Setting a filter resets the highlight to zero, so one Down lands on echo,
 which is option 4 of the full eleven and not option 1.

  line-confirm-filtered : Text =
    let dd = dropdown-nav-down (dropdown-set-filter (opened 0) "o")
    in let done = dropdown-confirm dd
    in "confirm filtered: highlight=" & show (dd.dd-highlight)
    & " chosen=[" & dropdown-selected-text done & "] index=" & show (done.dd-selected)

 A highlight past the end of the visible list must decline rather than
 choose. dropdown-with-selected seeds the highlight from an index into the
 FULL list, so a selection beyond the visible cap produces exactly that.

  line-confirm-beyond : Text =
    let dd = dropdown-toggle (dropdown-with-selected "dd" (opts 0) 10)
    in "confirm beyond cap: highlight=" & show (dd.dd-highlight)
    & " visible=" & show (list-length (dropdown-visible-options dd))
    & " kept=[" & dropdown-selected-text (dropdown-confirm dd) & "]"

Section: The keyboard

 UI chapter KeyInput settles what a key is in this quire: a character is
 its CCE code point and a named key is a constant at or above
 key-named-base. A handler testing 13, 32, 27, 38 and 40 is reading ASCII
 control codes and Windows virtual key codes, and in CCE those numbers are
 ordinary letters.

  line-key-open : Text =
    "key open: enter-on-closed=" & yn ((dropdown-handle-key (base 0) key-enter).dd-open)
    & " space-on-closed=" & yn ((dropdown-handle-key (base 0) (char-code ' ')).dd-open)
    & " letter-on-closed=" & yn ((dropdown-handle-key (base 0) (char-code 'q')).dd-open)

  line-key-nav : Text =
    "key nav: down=" & show ((dropdown-handle-key (opened 0) key-down).dd-highlight)
    & " then up=" & show ((dropdown-handle-key (dropdown-handle-key (opened 0) key-down) key-up).dd-highlight)

  line-key-escape : Text =
    "key escape: open-after=" & yn ((dropdown-handle-key (opened 0) key-escape).dd-open)

  line-key-confirm : Text =
    let dd = dropdown-handle-key (dropdown-handle-key (opened 0) key-down) key-enter
    in "key confirm: chosen=[" & dropdown-selected-text dd & "] open=" & yn (dd.dd-open)

Section: The widgets

  line-widget-closed : Text =
    "closed: none=" & payload (dropdown-widget (base 0))
    & " index2=" & payload (dropdown-widget (dropdown-with-selected "dd" (opts 0) 2))

  line-widget-open : Text =
    let w = dropdown-widget (opened 0)
    in "open: kids=" & show (w.wn-child-count)
    & " filter=" & payload (at w 0)
    & " items=" & show ((at w 1).wn-child-count)
    & " first=" & payload (at (at w 1) 0)

  line-format : Text =
    "format: [" & format-dropdown (dropdown-with-selected "dd" (opts 0) 2)
    & "] [" & format-dropdown (opened 0) & "]"

Section: Body

  report-a : Text =
    line-selected & "\n" & line-cap & "\n" & line-visible & "\n" & line-filtered

  report-b : Text =
    line-nav-clamp & "\n" & line-confirm & "\n" & line-confirm-filtered
    & "\n" & line-confirm-beyond

  report-c : Text =
    line-key-open & "\n" & line-key-nav & "\n" & line-key-escape & "\n" & line-key-confirm

  report-d : Text =
    line-widget-closed & "\n" & line-widget-open & "\n" & line-format

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni report-a
    print-line-uni report-b
    print-line-uni report-c
    print-line-uni report-d
  end
